<title>UK: UK's Brown says 3.5 bln stg to go to jobs plan.</title>
<headline>UK's Brown says 3.5 bln stg to go to jobs plan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said on Wednesday that he would spend 3.5 billion pounds from a windfall tax on Britain's privatised utilities to fund a welfare-to-work programme.</p>
<p>&quot;This programme of 3.5 billion pounds -- which includes an unallocated reserve of 500 million -- will be the main item funded from the windfall tax on the excess profits of the privatised utilities,&quot; he told parliament in his first budget speech.</p>
<p>The &quot;welfare-to-work&quot; programme is aimed at getting 250,000 young people off the dole.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
